{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1665","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"B. Array Cloning Technique"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given an array $$$a$$$ of $$$n$$$ integers. Initially there is only one copy of the given array."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You can do operations of two types:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":true},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Choose any array and clone it. After that there is one more copy of the chosen array. "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" Swap two elements from "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"any"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" two copies (maybe in the same copy) on any positions. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You need to find the minimal number of operations needed to obtain a copy where all elements are equal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The input consists of multiple test cases. The first line contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases. Description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 10^5$$$) — the length of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$-10^9 \\le a_i \\le 10^9$$$) — the elements of the array $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case output a single integer — the minimal number of operations needed to create at least one copy where all elements are equal."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n6\n1\n1789\n6\n0 1 3 3 7 0\n2\n-1000000000 1000000000\n4\n4 3 2 1\n5\n2 5 7 6 3\n7\n1 1 1 1 1 1 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n6\n2\n5\n7\n0\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case all elements in the array are already equal, that's why the answer is $$$0$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case it is possible to create a copy of the given array. After that there will be two identical arrays:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[ \\ 0 \\ 1 \\ 3 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$ and $$$[ \\ 0 \\ 1 \\ 3 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"After that we can swap elements in a way so all zeroes are in one array:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[ \\ 0 \\ \\underline{0} \\ \\underline{0} \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$ and $$$[ \\ \\underline{1} \\ 1 \\ 3 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ \\underline{3} \\ ]$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Now let's create a copy of the first array:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[ \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$, $$$[ \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$ and $$$[ \\ 1 \\ 1 \\ 3 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 3 \\ ]$$$"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Let's swap elements in the first two copies:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"$$$[ \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ 0 \\ \\underline{0} \\ \\underline{0} \\ 0 \\ ]$$$, $$$[ \\ \\underline{3} \\ \\underline{7} \\ 0 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 0 \\ ]$$$ and $$$[ \\ 1 \\ 1 \\ 3 \\ 3 \\ 7 \\ 3 \\ ]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Finally, we made a copy where all elements are equal and made $$$6$$$ operations."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It can be proven that no fewer operations are enough."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"B","problemCode":"1665B","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1665/problem/B"}